{"book":10,"chapter":23,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / THE LANGUAGE IN DEPTH / CHAPTER 23","slides":[{"title":"Real threads","sub":"Chapter 23 · No GIL, no races","short":"Intro","main":"OS threads on different cores; Rust forbids data races with types.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python: GIL","Rust: real threads","Data race"],"captions":["Python's global lock (GIL) keeps two threads from running Python code at once, so computations use processes","In Rust a thread is a real OS thread: each can run on its own core, with no global lock","Two threads write to the same memory and the result is random; Rust rejects such programs at build time"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"g","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"GIL","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 2 (waits)","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.6},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":120.0,"y1":88.0,"x2":160.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"c0","x":60.0,"y":60.0,"w":64.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 1","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c1","x":140.0,"y":60.0,"w":64.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 2","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c2","x":220.0,"y":60.0,"w":64.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 3","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c3","x":300.0,"y":60.0,"w":64.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 4","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"four cores, four threads","tone":"green","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":60.0,"h":34.0,"text":"x\n5","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":110.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 1: x = x + 1","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":290.0,"y":110.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"thread 2: x = x + 1","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":100.0,"y1":98.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":260.0,"y1":98.0,"x2":210.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":148.0,"text":"expected 7, got 6","tone":"red","size":9.0}]],"cues":[18.4,28.8]}]},{"title":"spawn, join, scope","sub":"Start and wait","short":"spawn","main":"spawn takes a move closure; join waits; scope lends local data.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["spawn","join","scope"],"captions":["thread::spawn runs a closure in a new thread; move hands the values over completely","join waits for the end and returns the result or a panic flag; otherwise main may finish before the threads","thread::scope lets threads take references to local data: the compiler knows scope waits for all of them"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let h = thread::spawn(move || {","    compute(data)","});"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"h: JoinHandle<T>","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":80.0,"y":50.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"main","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":80.0,"y":100.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"thread","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":134.0,"y1":112.0,"x2":234.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"j","x":280.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"h.join() → Ok(T)","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let mut v = vec![1, 2, 3];","thread::scope(|s| {","    s.spawn(|| println!(\"{:?}\", &v));","});   // all threads finished","v.push(4);"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[13.3,32.2]}]},{"title":"Behind spawn","sub":"clone, stack, scheduler","short":"Cost of a thread","main":"Each thread is a stack plus a scheduler entry; switching takes microseconds.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["The clone system call","Stack and queue","Switching"],"captions":["spawn asks the kernel for a new thread: on Linux that is the clone system call","The kernel allocates a stack (usually 2 MB of virtual memory), creates a task structure and puts it in the scheduler queue","Switching between threads takes microseconds: registers are saved and caches partly lost; a blocking call puts the thread to sleep"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"u","x":80.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"spawn (user space)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":134.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":224.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"k","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"clone() — kernel","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2 MB stack","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"task_struct","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"q","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":50.0,"text":"scheduler\nqueue\n[T1 T2 T3]","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":120.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":224.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":60.0,"y":50.0,"w":62.0,"h":26.0,"text":"T1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":130.0,"y":50.0,"w":62.0,"h":26.0,"text":"T2","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":200.0,"y":50.0,"w":62.0,"h":26.0,"text":"T1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t3","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":62.0,"h":26.0,"text":"T3","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"text":"context switch ≈ microseconds","size":9.5},{"t":"text","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":124.0,"text":"waits for network → kernel gives the CPU to another","tone":"green","size":9.0}]],"cues":[15.6,24.0]}]},{"title":"Send and Sync","sub":"What can be passed and shared","short":"Send and Sync","main":"Rc and RefCell do not cross a thread boundary — the compiler will not build it.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Rc is not Send","Arc — Send + Sync","Build error"],"captions":["Send — a value can be passed to another thread; Sync — a reference can be shared. Rc's counter uses plain addition — two threads would corrupt it","Arc counts atomically, so it is Send + Sync (if its contents are too)","spawn requires Send from the closure: an Rc will not get into a thread — the compiler stops the build"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Rc<T>: !Send","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"RefCell<T>: !Sync","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"non-atomic counters and flags","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Arc<T>: Send + Sync","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Mutex<T>: Sync","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"atomic / under a lock","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let rc = Rc::new(5);","thread::spawn(move || println!(\"{rc}\"));","// error: `Rc<i32>` cannot be sent between threads"],"hl":[1,2],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":20.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[14.4,25.4]}]},{"title":"Mutex","sub":"Data inside a lock","short":"Mutex","main":"Mutex<T> owns the data; the guard releases the lock in drop.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Data inside a mutex","The guard","Poisoning"],"captions":["Mutex<T> owns the data: you can reach the value only through lock() — you cannot forget to protect it","lock() returns a guard; while it lives the data is yours alone, and drop at the end of scope releases the lock itself","If a thread panics while holding the lock, the mutex is poisoned: the next lock() returns Err, which can be handled"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":160.0,"h":60.0,"text":"","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":46.0,"text":"Mutex","size":9.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":180.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"value T","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let counter = Arc::new(Mutex::new(0));","{","    let mut g = counter.lock().unwrap();","    *g += 1;","}   // guard destroyed — lock is free"],"hl":[2,4],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"thread panics\nunder the lock","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":134.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":224.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"PoisonError\n(data still accessible)","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| e.into_inner())","size":8.5,"mono":true}]],"cues":[13.4,28.0]}]},{"title":"RwLock","sub":"Readers or a writer","short":"RwLock","main":"Many readers or one writer — like the cache protocol.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Many readers","One writer","Like caches"],"captions":["RwLock allows any number of readers at once — while nobody writes","The writer waits until all readers leave and works alone; the others wait for it","Same idea as MESI: shared state for reading and exclusive for writing — at the program level"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"data","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r0","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"reads","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cel